gDescription":"ThinkVision Control is an unofficial app that controls a Lenovo ThinkVision P32p-20 from the computer instead of its buttons, over DDC/CI.\nIt puts the whole on-screen menu in one small window: input switching (HDMI, DisplayPort, USB-C), brightness and contrast, Day and Night presets, colour mode, Over Drive, Dynamic Contrast, aspect ratio, USB charging, menu language and resets.\nIt adds global keyboard shortcuts with an on-screen indicator, a tray menu, automatic Day/Night at set times or at sunrise and sunset, a \"Switch to this PC\" action for monitors shared between two computers, a command line (--preset, --input, --step, --get) and thinkvision:// links.\nNot affiliated with Lenovo. Lenovo and ThinkVision are trademarks of Lenovo.","moniker":"thinkvision-control","name":"ThinkVision Control","packageUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan/thinkvision-control","publisher":"MrErrorSan","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan/thinkvision-control/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan","releaseNotes":"Fixed: the app didn't start on some Windows PCs. 0.0.5 and 0.0.6 needed the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable, which a fresh Windows doesn't have; the program now carries everything it needs.\nReleases are now built by GitHub Actions from the tagged source.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan/thinkvision-control/releases/tag/v0.0.7","tags":["brightness","contrast","ddc","ddc-ci","display","lenovo","monitor","thinkvision"]}},"publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan/thinkvision-control/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan","releaseDate":"2026-11-13","releaseDateSource":"commit","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/MrErrorSan/thinkvision-control/releases/tag/v0.0.7","schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","upstream":{"commit":"e72b66ccfdee8a8345772e98de181e2086fd56ec","manifestVersion":"1.28.0","manifests":[{"path":"manifests/m/MrErrorSan/ThinkVisionControl/0.0.7/MrErrorSan.ThinkVisionCont